# <type>[(optional scope)]: <short summary, imperative mood, lowercase, no trailing period>
#
# Types (see CONTRIBUTING.md "Commit Messages: Conventional Commits"):
#   feat fix docs test refactor chore perf build ci
# Add "!" after the type/scope (e.g. "feat!:") or a "BREAKING CHANGE:" footer below for
# anything breaking a published contract — check AGENTS.md §8 for whether it also needs an RFC.
#
# --- Body (optional, blank line above) ---
# Explain *why*, not *what* — the diff already shows what changed. Wrap around ~90 chars.
#
# --- Footer (blank line above) ---
# BREAKING CHANGE: <what breaks, and the migration path>
# Refs: #<issue-number>       (work in progress against the issue)
# Closes: #<issue-number>     (this commit/PR resolves it)
#
# Every commit traces to an open issue — find one or `gh issue create` before your first
# commit, then reference it here. Not optional; see .github/CONTRIBUTING_AGENT.md.
#
# One logical, reviewable change per commit — not the whole task in one commit. See
# .github/CONTRIBUTING_AGENT.md for the branch + commit workflow this repo expects.
#
# This template is enabled per-clone, not globally, by design (see Git Safety Protocol) — run:
#   git config commit.template .gitmessage
